# CAE research workbench tools

Connect to the already running shared CAE service. Read supported backend inputs,
existing results and authorized sources before proposing a fit, DOE, optimization
or solver run. A study and CAD are optional. Keep native execution, imported
results and external file exchange distinct. Missing results remain unknown.

Use the numerical libraries for samples, residuals, search and influence. Preserve
units, components, locations and event meaning. Submit only within the user's
approved input ranges, evaluation budget, resources and data transmission scope.
Read the shared job ID and actual result before claiming completion. Cancellation
is a request until the shared controller confirms a terminal state.

The user's host selects its model and authentication independently. This example
sets no model, fixed expert/domain list or tool count. Optional expert roles are
configured separately; absent internal inference remains NOT_CONFIGURED. A
numerical fit or expert agreement does not establish physical qualification.
